INTRODUCTION:
This week's work focuses on the initial representation and exploration of the Autoimmune Disorder dataset as part of the Data Science and Visualization (DSV) project. The purpose of this stage is to understand the structure, characteristics, and contents of the dataset before performing detailed data analysis and visualization.
The dataset contains patient information, autoimmune disorder diagnoses, blood and laboratory measurements, symptoms, and different antibody-related test results.

DATASET DESCRIPTION:
The project uses the Autoimmune Disorder dataset, containing 12,500 patient records and 78 attributes.
Each record represents a patient, while the columns contain information such as:
•	Patient ID
•	Age and Gender
•	Diagnosis
•	Sickness duration
•	Blood-related measurements
•	Immune and inflammatory
•	Symptoms
•	Autoantibody test results
The dataset contains 116 different diagnosis categories, including normal cases and various autoimmune disorders.
OBJECTIVES:
The main objectives of Week 2 were to load and understand the Autoimmune Disorder dataset, inspect its structure and dimensions, identify the available attributes, distinguish numerical and categorical attributes, examine the basic statistical characteristics of numerical variables, understand patient symptoms and laboratory measurements, represent the dataset in a structured manner, and prepare it for further exploratory data analysis and visualization.

