DATASET LOADING:
The dataset was loaded into a Pandas DataFrame. Each row represents a patient, while each column represents an attribute or feature associated with that patient. The cleaned dataset contains 12,500 rows and 78 columns, providing information about patient demographics, diagnoses, clinical measurements, symptoms, and antibody-related features.
DATASET REPRESENTATION:
The initial records of the dataset were examined using df.head(), while the final records can be inspected using df.tail(). The dimensions of the dataset were examined using df.shape. The dataset contains 12,500 patient records and 78 attributes, including demographic information, diagnosis information, laboratory measurements, symptoms, and antibody-related features.
DATASET STRUCTURE:
The structure and data types of the columns were examined using df.info(). The dataset contains both categorical and numerical attributes. Categorical attributes include Gender and Diagnosis, while numerical attributes include Age, Sickness Duration, RBC Count, Haemoglobin, Haematocrit, MCV, MCH, MCHC, RDW, WBC Count, Platelet Count, ESR, C3, C4, and CRP. The dataset also contains binary features representing symptoms and antibody test results, which are generally encoded as 0 and 1.
