DATA REPRESENTATION THROUGH VISUALISATION:
Visualization provides an intuitive understanding of the autoimmune disorder dataset. Histograms and KDE plots 
can be used to represent distributions of important numerical features such as Age, Hemoglobin, ESR, and CRP. Bar
charts and count plots can be used to represent the distribution of diagnosis categories, gender, and symptoms.
Box plots can be used to compare laboratory measurements across different diagnoses, while scatter plots can help 
examine relationships between variables. Heatmaps can also be used to study correlations between numerical features.
These visualizations help identify patterns, distributions, relationships, and unusual observations in the dataset.

